🧩 LEVEL 1: Basic Traversal & Manipulation Patterns
Goal: Understand how to access, loop, and modify elements.
| # | Pattern Name              | Concept                       | Example Problem                 |
| - | ------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| 1 | **Traversal**             | Loop through all elements     | Print all elements of an array  |
| 2 | **Reverse Traversal**     | Iterate from end to start     | Print array in reverse          |
| 3 | **Sum / Product Pattern** | Aggregate elements            | Find sum or average of elements |
| 4 | **Find Min / Max**        | Compare elements              | Find largest/smallest element   |
| 5 | **Counting / Frequency**  | Use counter arrays or HashMap | Count frequency of numbers      |

🧠 Learn skill: Basic for-loops, conditions, and thinking in indexes.

⚙️ LEVEL 2: Conditional & Two-Pointer Patterns
Goal: Learn how to reduce complexity and handle pairs efficiently.
| #  | Pattern Name                   | Concept                     | Example Problem                              |
| -- | ------------------------------ | --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| 6  | **Two Sum Pattern**            | Check pairs with sum target | Find if two numbers add to `k`               |
| 7  | **Two Pointers Opposite Ends** | Shrinking window            | Check if array is palindrome                 |
| 8  | **Sliding Window**             | Maintain window sum         | Find max sum of subarray of size k           |
| 9  | **Prefix Sum**                 | Precompute running totals   | Find subarray sum quickly                    |
| 10 | **Difference Array**           | Range updates               | Increment values in given ranges efficiently |

🧠 Learn skill: Optimize O(n²) → O(n) using smart traversal.

🧮 LEVEL 3: Searching & Sorting Patterns
Goal: Learn to organize data efficiently.
| #  | Pattern Name              | Concept                         | Example Problem                |
| -- | ------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| 11 | **Binary Search Pattern** | Divide & conquer search         | Search element in sorted array |
| 12 | **Sorting & Two-Pointer** | Combine sorting with scanning   | 3Sum, Merge intervals          |
| 13 | **Partitioning Pattern**  | Divide array based on condition | Dutch National Flag Problem    |
| 14 | **Cyclic Sort Pattern**   | Sorting when values are 1..N    | Find missing number            |

🧠 Learn skill: Thinking in sorted space and mathematical reasoning.

🔁 LEVEL 4: Subarray / Subsequence Patterns
Goal: Handle parts of arrays and build logic for dynamic problems.
| #  | Pattern Name                             | Concept                | Example Problem                |
| -- | ---------------------------------------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| 15 | **Kadane’s Algorithm**                   | Maximum subarray sum   | Max sum of contiguous subarray |
| 16 | **All Subarrays Generation**             | Nested loops           | Print all subarrays            |
| 17 | **Subsequence Generation**               | Recursive pattern      | Generate all subsequences      |
| 18 | **Longest Increasing Subsequence (LIS)** | DP pattern             | Find LIS length                |
| 19 | **Prefix Min/Max Arrays**                | Precompute useful info | Trapping rain water problem    |
🧠 Learn skill: Break large problems into overlapping subproblems.

🧠 LEVEL 5: Advanced & Interview Patterns
Goal: Build confidence with real interview logic.

| #  | Pattern Name                    | Concept         | Example Problem                     |
| -- | ------------------------------- | --------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| 20 | **Matrix Patterns (2D arrays)** | Nested loops    | Rotate matrix, spiral print         |
| 21 | **Merge Intervals Pattern**     | Interval logic  | Merge overlapping intervals         |
| 22 | **Monotonic Stack Pattern**     | Stack + array   | Next Greater Element                |
| 23 | **Fast & Slow Pointers**        | Detect cycles   | Linked list / array cycle detection |
| 24 | **Bit Manipulation Pattern**    | Binary thinking | Find single non-duplicate element   |
🧠 Learn skill: Pattern recognition + optimization techniques.


🚀 How to Learn Step-by-Step
Pick one pattern per day.
Practice 2–3 problems of that type on LeetCode or GeeksForGeeks.
Write brute force → optimize → dry run.
Maintain an “Array Pattern Notes” file:
Pattern name
Example
Key idea
Template code

